{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And each man loaded his donkey.</b> They were men of arm — and had no need to help one another load." "<b>And they returned to the city.</b> It was a metropolis, yet he says הָעִירָה — 'the city,' any city at all; only, in their eyes for purposes of war it counted as no more than an ordinary town of ten men."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:28.036779163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}